# ...except this one.  m6_calibration.py and extract_pls.py both read it, so
# a clean checkout that does not have it reports a DIFFERENT number of checks
# than the workstation does -- and a check count that depends on the machine
# is not a check.  It is a verification input, not an analysis leftover.
!data/properties/M5_c26k_T1000_ss.csv
# ...and these three, for the same reason and one more.  a1 asked for them so
# figure 4.6 (b)(c) can be a real curve instead of a verdict bar (a1-0039).
# They then became a verification input too: m6_report and m6_verdict fit the
# settled tangent on them and assert that the rejected fractional definition
# drifts +9.1 % under truncation.  Without the files that is not a check, it
# is a check that skips itself on a clean checkout.
!data/results/M6/LTH_M6_RT23_ss.csv
!data/results/M6/LTH_M6_T500_ss.csv
!data/results/M6/LTH_M6_T1000_ss.csv
ss_curves_by_temperature.png
dist/*.pdf
